>In addition to the other good advice, I'd add:
>1) I'd recommend that you avoid increasing your XP beyond 14.  

  I'd recommend getting to XL:30 and then keep going.  Gaining levels
won't take you past XL:30, but you'll still get Hp and Mana gains.  Pw
gains depend on Wis, so max that out and wear a max enchanted Helm of
Brilliance when leveling up.

>When at
>14 you will have available the beginning Quest levels where you might
>find some useful equipment.  

  Increasing XL is very important for a Wizard.  Damage caused by
Magic Missile depends directly on XL.  Skill slots for #enhancing
spell skills for lower failure rates and better effects (e.g. cone of
cold and jumping).  Higher XL lowers failure rates all by itself.
Gaining XL increases Hp and Pw.  (Wizards want Power.)

>But, in general increasing your XP at this stage will make your 
>life more difficult.  

  Once the Invocation is done the dungeon level used for determining
difficulty of monsters generated is fixed at the level of Moloch's
Sanctum, for the rest of the game.   Better to find out early if you
can deal with that level of monster for long periods of time.  

  Not to mention that the extra skill slots, Hp, and mana will help
deal with the tougher monsters.  Remember, those tougher opponents are
going to show up no matter what your XL is, so it's better to prepare
for them early.  (Gaining 16 XL immediately after doing the Invocation
is difficult.)

>You have charm monster; charm some useful creatures and let them gain 
>the experience.

  The success rate of the spell of Charm Monster depends on character
XL.

>2) Do you have reflection yet?  It only takes one lucky @ with a wand
>of death to end your game.

  Not with Magic Resistance.  Wizards end up with three guaranteed
sources of MR: Starting cloak of MR, wielded Magicbane, the Eye of the
Aethiopica.  A smart player will use all three.

>3) Start collecting gold and gain some intrinsic AC.  It weighs
>nothing!

  Yes.  Then hold a sacrifest to gain more divine protection (among
other things).  Don't try to buy down below naked AC of 1.  You'll
want to save that money for when you lose divine AC (which I generally
do at least once a game.)



